      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The slip-to-twinning transition is sensitive to crystallographic loading direction.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The slip-to-twinning transition is sensitive to temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The slip-to-twinning transition is sensitive to strain rate.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial Co-free FeNiCrMn alloy is equiatomic.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial Co-free FeNiCrMn alloy is a single-phase solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures and slower strain rates, deformation is dominated by dislocation slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation-slip-dominated deformation produces higher ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher temperatures promote mechanical twinning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Faster strain rates promote mechanical twinning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crystallographic orientations favorable for twin nucleation increase twinning activity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased twinning raises yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased twinning reduces ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the room-temperature, moderate-strain-rate, [100] baseline, dislocation slip is the dominant mechanism.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, twinning-promoting conditions will increase yield strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, twinning-promoting conditions will decrease strain to failure or ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The prediction is intended to apply only below the onset of phase transformation and while dislocation slip and twinning remain the primary deformation mechanisms.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
